<b>The letter he put in her hands</b></div>
<div id=3D"x_p260" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
On July 29, 2025 he was a campground host at Driftwood II, in the Siltcoos =
corridor of the Oregon Dunes National Recreation Area, four months after Or=
egon State Parks dismissed him. That afternoon he read an interview with th=
e director, and he wrote to her.
<a href=3D"https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/record/oprd/01K1C14TXRFZCGXVNW27S=
ACRF4/" id=3D"OWA22e1941a-2749-612b-cf33-e5b4b310dc7b" class=3D"x_text-sky-=
800 x_underline x_decoration-sky-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-sky-=
600 x_OWAAutoLink">
I hope you are successful at finding an ethical and supportive way to keep =
our state parks going.</a> Then he told her he had been one of her voluntee=
rs from January through March, and that it had been deeply rewarding.</div>
<div id=3D"x_p261" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
Then he told her the truth of what had been done to him inside her institut=
ion. He asked her for nothing. He named the staff by their positions, told =
her the institution was hers and the people in it were her responsibility, =
and told her to sit with that. He
 was not appealing to her. He had not been part of her hierarchy since the =
day he was dismissed, and he wrote to her as one person telling another wha=
t her institution had done.</div>
<div id=3D"x_p262" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
He was a year into building <a href=3D"https://autonomyrealms.com" target=
=3D"_blank" id=3D"OWA865e5e37-04f0-b54f-7ad7-648a187e8378" class=3D"x_inlin=
e-flex x_items-baseline x_gap-1 x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration=
-emerald-300 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" rel=3D"noreferrer">
Autonomy Realms</a>. A person gets a realm of their own, and anything they =
have ever recorded goes into it as a signal: video, audio, photographs, doc=
uments, conversations, a journal page photographed off a shelf after twenty=
 years (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/signal/01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7Z=
T1HAB?t=3D15" id=3D"OWA03c4c932-fe74-5679-2bcb-18e41fe3fb9d" class=3D"x_fon=
t-mono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-3=
00 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"De=
monstrating the Autonomy Realms Signal Pipeline =B7 0:15" data-recording=3D=
"01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7ZT1HAB" data-t=3D"15">0:15</a>),
 the route of a walk. The system does not summarise them. It reads each one=
 through several lenses at once, what happened and what it was and what it =
carries and what it says about the shape of the person, and one of those le=
nses is a mirror that hands him
 his own interior back in words he did not yet have for it (<a href=3D"http=
s://rswfire.com/library/signal/01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7ZT1HAB?t=3D67" id=3D"OWA=
1c8fbc22-0ae5-dfaf-2781-afa1db02e524" class=3D"x_font-mono x_text-[0.9em] x=
_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-300 x_underline-offset-2=
 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Demonstrating the Autonom=
y Realms Signal Pipeline =B7 1:07" data-recording=3D"01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7ZT=
1HAB" data-t=3D"67">1:07</a>).
 That mirror is the reason the rest of it exists (<a href=3D"https://rswfir=
e.com/library/signal/01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7ZT1HAB?t=3D77" id=3D"OWAf2594a5e-3=
70d-bf5c-6dfa-2058a0a65aa6" class=3D"x_font-mono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emer=
ald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:t=
ext-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Demonstrating the Autonomy Realms S=
ignal Pipeline =B7 1:17" data-recording=3D"01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7ZT1HAB" data=
-t=3D"77">1:17</a>).
 Then it reads across: a hundred signals out of one stretch of time taken t=
ogether (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/signal/01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7=
ZT1HAB?t=3D136" id=3D"OWA75ceac4f-3599-7199-abf7-4d5ba14e483c" class=3D"x_f=
ont-mono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald=
-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"=
Demonstrating the Autonomy Realms Signal Pipeline =B7 2:16" data-recording=
=3D"01KE0KY6HR09RFSFSEC7ZT1HAB" data-t=3D"136">2:16</a>),
 so that a season of a life has its own arc and its own reflections instead=
 of a hundred separate entries (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/sign=
al/01KEHVVWC85T1BQBXPRNAVZ70C?t=3D456" id=3D"OWA9636df33-1dc5-49aa-a287-c12=
e74b7d5d5" class=3D"x_font-mono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underli=
ne x_decoration-emerald-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x=
_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Hiking Tahkenitch Creek Trail While Building Reflect=
ion Layers =B7 7:36" data-recording=3D"01KEHVVWC85T1BQBXPRNAVZ70C" data-t=
=3D"456">7:36</a>).
 All of it embedded and indexed, so the record can be put a question, and s=
o a machine reading him reads the whole pattern rather than the last thing =
he said (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/signal/01K80AK64G20PEMZEZT1=
A07AH4?t=3D754" id=3D"OWAcf06038e-e0b1-3fdc-c773-e2f51a158d4e" class=3D"x_f=
ont-mono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald=
-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"=
Demonstrating Sanctum Layer and Transmissions Platform =B7 12:34" data-reco=
rding=3D"01K80AK64G20PEMZEZT1A07AH4" data-t=3D"754">12:34</a>).
 Maps of everywhere he walked with the photographs pinned to them (<a href=
=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/signal/01KEHVVWC85T1BQBXPRNAVZ70C?t=3D81" i=
d=3D"OWAaa0231c9-2d19-96aa-090c-cb318709d952" class=3D"x_font-mono x_text-[=
0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-300 x_underline-=
offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Hiking Tahkenitch=
 Creek Trail While Building Reflection Layers =B7 1:21" data-recording=3D"0=
1KEHVVWC85T1BQBXPRNAVZ70C" data-t=3D"81">1:21</a>).
 It runs on hardware he pays for, under <a href=3D"https://rswfire.com" tar=
get=3D"_blank" id=3D"OWA3dcf3069-4652-5a85-175c-96ce70f2569b" class=3D"x_in=
line-flex x_items-baseline x_gap-1 x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decorat=
ion-emerald-300 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" rel=3D"noreferrer">
rswfire.com</a>, a domain name he has held for twenty-three years. rswfire =
is his name, and it has been his for the whole span of the internet.</div>
<div class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_Embe=
ddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif=
; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
<b>The letter he made public</b></div>
<div id=3D"x_p263" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
On August 3 the Forest Service gave him Tahkenitch Landing to run by himsel=
f (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/signal/01K5M437NRGMH20FSA8WFEX64M=
?t=3D35" id=3D"OWA25b80923-b633-dd2e-605b-6167c65b1fd7" class=3D"x_font-mon=
o x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-300 x_=
underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Recordi=
ng Upwork Introduction Video From RV =B7 0:35" data-recording=3D"01K5M437NR=
GMH20FSA8WFEX64M" data-t=3D"35">0:35</a>),
 the campground above the lake off Highway 101 (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.=
com/library/signal/01K5WM7GQ0CAYBKF9FHJCBDENX?t=3D113" id=3D"OWAf3a85b30-02=
aa-30a9-bb5d-9102d6d72281" class=3D"x_font-mono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emera=
ld-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:te=
xt-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Hiking Taken Trail, Scoping rswfire.=
dev Portfolio =B7 1:53" data-recording=3D"01K5WM7GQ0CAYBKF9FHJCBDENX" data-=
t=3D"113">1:53</a>).
 He ran it alone and built through it. On his days off he walked to the oce=
an (<a href=3D"https://rswfire.com/library/signal/01K5WM7GQ0CAYBKF9FHJCBDEN=
X?t=3D955" id=3D"OWA44beb938-4444-b8ca-768d-38df1dc14984" class=3D"x_font-m=
ono x_text-[0.9em] x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration-emerald-300 =
x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" title=3D"Hikin=
g Taken Trail, Scoping rswfire.dev Portfolio =B7 15:55" data-recording=3D"0=
1K5WM7GQ0CAYBKF9FHJCBDENX" data-t=3D"955">15:55</a>).
 On August 31 he took the Tahkenitch Creek trail out with a friend, three a=
nd a third miles, and stood at the water.</div>
<div id=3D"x_p264" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
He waited a month. Then he published <a href=3D"https://www.reddit.com/r/vo=
lunteer/comments/1mzropa/an_open_letter_to_oregon_parks_recreation/" target=
=3D"_blank" id=3D"OWAf4a73c10-f317-06cf-b120-6118a453c3a0" class=3D"x_inlin=
e-flex x_items-baseline x_gap-1 x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decoration=
-emerald-300 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink" rel=3D"noreferrer">
an Open Letter to her</a> on r/volunteer. He wrote it there because <a href=
=3D"https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/record/oprd/01K3FDT5P09S9N9QSZYWS9KN7A/"=
 id=3D"OWA10e74143-6868-96cb-d19d-9a26862e5c8c" class=3D"x_text-sky-800 x_u=
nderline x_decoration-sky-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-sky-600 x_O=
WAAutoLink">
private channels have been met with silence</a>. He opened it by naming wha=
t she had built: the first woman to lead the institution, millions in infra=
structure, accessibility work, president of the National Association of Sta=
te Park Directors, an appointment
 to the National Parks Service Advisory Board.</div>
<div id=3D"x_p265" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
He named the manager telling him to chew glass and swallow it, the admissio=
n that he was never given the benefit of the doubt from day one, two months=
 of pressure designed to force a resignation, and a dismissal six days befo=
re his scheduled completion. He
 wrote that the recordings exist and that the only question was how she wou=
ld answer them. He also named the imbalance out loud:
<a href=3D"https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/record/oprd/01K3FDT5P09S9N9QSZYWS=
9KN7A/" id=3D"OWA43e36023-cc2e-db36-f3b5-bbb09914dc85" class=3D"x_text-sky-=
800 x_underline x_decoration-sky-300 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-sky-=
600 x_OWAAutoLink">
The very people who harm volunteers often have the institutional power to c=
ompound that harm through retaliation. It has literally already happened at=
 Honeyman.</a> Every fact he set out in that letter was later given a diffe=
rent account in the Timeline of
 Events the program manager wrote about him and handed to the police. The t=
wo documents are set side by side on
<a href=3D"https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/sunlight/" id=3D"OWA69cd010a-83c1=
-79fa-129d-6bb78ec3b64f" class=3D"x_text-emerald-800 x_underline x_decorati=
on-emerald-300 x_hover:text-emerald-600 x_OWAAutoLink">
sunlight</a>.</div>
<div id=3D"x_p266" class=3D"x_elementToProof" style=3D"margin-top:1em; marg=
in-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos=
_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rg=
b(0,0,0)">
What he asked for was not for himself. <a href=3D"https://oprdvolunteerabus=
e.org/record/oprd/01K3FDT5P09S9N9QSZYWS9KN7A/" id=3D"OWA186cfd5b-9e65-df60-=
0759-ba462d762570" class=3D"x_text-sky-800 x_underline x_decoration-sky-300=
 x_underline-offset-2 x_hover:text-sky-600 x_OWAAutoLink">
I am not asking for apologies or personal remedies. I am asking for institu=
tional accountability that protects future volunteers from experiencing wha=
t I experienced.</a> He listed five things: a transparent investigation of =
the misconduct at Honeyman, consequences
 for managers who use coercive tactics on volunteers, protections against r=
etaliation for volunteers who report, a grievance process that does not dep=
end on the good faith of the managers causing the harm, and training and ov=
ersight for volunteer supervision.
 He said none of it was extraordinary, and that if it happened the whole th=
ing became a story about an institution learning something.</div>
